Subject: [PATCH] Ayaneo Pocket DS: the rotation of the second panel is not written to Settings.System

While the second (bottom) panel is the default display (bottom screen only, or screens swapped),
SystemUI's rotation watcher saved "locked at 270" into Settings.System, the setting of the main
panel: back on the top panel the screen stayed in portrait. The rotation of the second panel
stays in the display settings.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayRotation.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayRotation.java
index 4c43176b5..0594ff6fd 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayRotation.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayRotation.java
@@ -814,7 +814,11 @@ public class DisplayRotation {
 
     @VisibleForTesting
     void setUserRotation(int userRotationMode, int userRotation, String caller) {
-        if (useDefaultSettingsProvider()) {
+        // Ayaneo Pocket DS: while the default display is the second panel (bottom screen only,
+        // or screens swapped), its rotation is kept apart (display settings): writing it into
+        // Settings.System would leave the top panel with the rotation of the bottom one once
+        // it is the default display again.
+        if (useDefaultSettingsProvider() && !mAyaneoPanelRotation) {
             // We'll be notified via settings listener, so we don't need to update internal values.
             final ContentResolver res = mContext.getContentResolver();
             final int accelerometerRotation =
